  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes cross-drill topology depending on floating-point roundoff: a stock radius of `next_up(10.0)` previously produced 14 moves rather than 13 for `10.0`.\r\n\r\n- Coalesce only radial rapid targets within `1e-9 mm` of the current tip. Still call `PathBuilder::push` so stationary pose changes remain represented.\r\n- Leave the shared CL builder, cutting moves, stock measurements and stock/holder/part safety proofs unchanged.\r\n- Replace raw-float hashes with fixed ordered numeric reference chains captured before the correction. Counts, kinds, feeds and poses stay strict; only endpoint coordinates receive tolerance.\r\n- Cover near-equal radii, real clearance movement, stationary indexing and multiple G54 translations on lathe and mill-turn.\r\n\r\n## Review follow-up\r\n\r\nPreserves the maintainer's integration commit `254a95cf2206c0ab260602d11fcc4664f802963b`, including main's whole-hole `traverse_s` calls and chord solver, with this PR's `rapid()` wrapper. The decision entry now lives in `docs/decisions/151-cross-drill-invariance.md`; `RECOMMENDED.md` equals upstream main. The only follow-up edit after that integration documents the cost to change the decision later.\r\n\r\nIntegrated main: `5208e94015239c8c05c53b8d78e84f1a8cf6e3bf`.\r\nRuntime-tested tree: `70848014f550e46a9cfa3bb4fc32c6f9a411cbd4`.\r\nFinal reviewed tree: `e0c513137a51cfab6d47eeb7b0d52fdb9ca936fd`.\r\n\r\nAn exact Git comparison shows these trees differ only in the per-PR decision Markdown. Every source, test, build input and dependency file is identical. Runtime receipts therefore apply to the unchanged executable inputs; they are not represented as a new test run on the documentation-only commit. The full six-file PR delta has been independently reviewed, with the documentation follow-up checked separately.\r\n\r\n## Focused quick-tier validation - native Windows\r\n\r\nAll four direct Cargo processes exited **0**, with **58 passed / 0 failed / 0 ignored** across five libtest result blocks:\r\n\r\n| Suite | Passed |\r\n|---|---:|\r\n| motion lib, `drilling` filter | 34 |\r\n| motion `cross_invariance` | 2 |\r\n| app `drilling_cross_box` | 7 |\r\n| app `drilling_cross_spindle` | 7 |\r\n| app `drilling_cross_stock`, including #81 off-centre chord coverage | 8 |\r\n\r\nCommands (run with `--locked -j 6`; test commands also used `-- --test-threads=6`):\r\n\r\n```text\r\ncargo test --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --lib drilling -- --test-threads=6\r\ncargo test --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --test cross_invariance -- --test-threads=6\r\ncargo test --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-app --test drilling_cross_box --test drilling_cross_spindle --test drilling_cross_stock -- --test-threads=6\r\ncargo clippy --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings\r\n```\r\n\r\nSelected affected binaries per the review request and repository's test-the-change policy; this is not a rerun of the automatic full-app quick selector. The shared numeric fixture is unchanged in this follow-up. Source tree and Cargo.lock were preserved; totals were independently recomputed from complete logs. The remote Shell wrapper timed out, but the persistent runner completed and captured each actual Cargo return code; no outer runner exit code is claimed.\r\n\r\n## Historical evidence and limits\r\n\r\nThe regression was reproduced before correction (13 versus 14 moves; 1 passed / 1 failed). The previous submitted tree `8dae5e8129e9b7f193f4bc576fc57a22d73d1f33` passed its canonical quick gate (1,173 passed / 0 failed / 17 ignored) and motion/sim/app Clippy, all with captured exit 0. Those broad-suite results are historical, not execution on this updated integration. Earlier receipts, including the original quick-wrapper exit caveat, remain preserved.\r\n\r\nmacOS and Linux x86_64 were NOT RUN. Supplementary Linux aarch64 compilation stopped before tests in unchanged Flecs `c_char` bindings; no dependency workaround is included. Full release/heavy lanes and production NC execution were not performed. No hosted checks are reported; no workflow was enabled or dispatched.\r\n\r\nThis remains the sole replacement for closed, unmerged #236 after its stacked base branch was deleted. No deleted branch was recreated. No new dependency, file format change, protected-main merge, auto-merge or release.\r\n\r\nReadings: #151 and maintainer feedback, current repository instructions, radial generator, shared PathBuilder semantics, relevant stock/holder/part proof call paths and actual baseline numeric chains. Original synthetic fixtures and elementary floating-point/Euclidean comparison only; no vendor implementation material.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Avoid roundoff-only cross-drill rapids while preserving station poses and portable numeric-chain regressions.\r\n\r\nFixes #151\r\n",
